}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Graceful Degradation:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li720\fi0 {\pntext\pard\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 If a dependent service fails, }{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 degrade functionality}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2  without crashing the whole service.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Circuit Breaker Pattern:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li720\fi0 {\pntext\pard\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Prevents continuous requests to a failing service by }{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 cutting off communication temporarily}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 .\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li720\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Example:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2  If Service A fails, the circuit breaker stops Service B from making further requests, preventing further cascading failures.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Fallback Mechanisms:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li720\fi0 {\pntext\pard\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Provide }{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 alternative responses}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2  when dependencies fail.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li720\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Example:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2  If a weather service fails, return }{\dbch\af2\loch\f5\fs40\cf2 "Weather data is currently unavailable"}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs24\cf2  }{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs36\cf2 instead of crashing the service.}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs64\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Timeouts and Retries:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li720\fi0 {\pntext\pard\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Implement }{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 timeouts}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2  to avoid waiting indefinitely for a response from a failing service.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li720\fi0 {\pntext\pard\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 Use }{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 limited retries}{\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2  to handle temporary failures.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li540\fi-540\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033 {\dbch\af2\loch\f4 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li540\fi-540\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\b\shad\f1\fs48\cf1 Determining and Handling Failures in Microservice Architecture\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs53 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs53{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs48\cf2 Introduction to Failure Detection\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs53 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs53{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs48\cf2 In a microservice-based system, determining when a dependency is failing is crucial to prevent cascading service failures and ensure application stability. However, different types of failures require different detection techniques, and each type of failure demands a tailored response.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li540\fi-540\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\b\shad\f1\fs56\cf1 Failure Modes in Microservices\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs44 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Failures can manifest in several ways, ordered from easiest to hardest to detect:\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Garbled Response}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 The response is in an unrecognizable or corrupted format (e.g., syntax errors).\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Immediate detection is possible since the data is unreadable.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Response Indicated a Fatal Error}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 A response contains information about a critical failure within the service (e.g., invalid request or internal processing error).\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 This failure typically occurs within the service logic, not the communication layer.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Unexpected Results}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 The operation executes successfully, but the data returned is incorrect or unexpected.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li540\fi-540\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\b\shad\f1\fs56\cf1 Failure Modes in Microservices\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 4. Result Out of Expected Bounds}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 The data is in the correct format but falls outside the reasonable or expected range.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Example: If the number of days since January 1 is returned as 843, it\'92s out of a plausible range.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 5. No Response\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li630\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 The request is sent, but no response is received.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li630\fi0 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Possible causes: network issues, service crash, or service outage.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 6. Slow Response\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 The response arrives but takes longer than expected, possibly due to network congestion or resource exhaustion.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 It is the hardest to handle since timing can be inconsistent.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li630\fi0 {\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs64\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs64\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li540\fi-540\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\b\shad\f1\fs56\cf1 Handling Detected Failures\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs44 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Different failure modes call for specific strategies to maintain stability and usability.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 3.1 Graceful Degradation: }{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 If a service dependency fails, perform partial operations to maintain functionality.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s4\li2250\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1710 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs40 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Example:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2  Display cached or limited data if a backend service is unavailable.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 3.2 Graceful Backoff: }{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 When failure renders continued operation impossible, find an alternative, less impactful way to respond.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s4\li2250\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1710 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs40 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Example:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2  Redirect users to a maintenance page with relevant messaging instead of a generic error.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs44 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs44{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 3.3 Fail as Early as Possible: }{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 If a request is certain to fail, halt further processing immediately to save resources.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s4\li2250\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1710 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs40 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 Example:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2  Check for invalid inputs (like division by zero) at the earliest step to prevent complex failures later.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs40\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li540\fi-540\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\b\shad\f1\fs56\cf1 Handling Detected Failures\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs62 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs62{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2 Why Fail Early?\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs62 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs62{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2 Resource Conservation:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2  Prevent unnecessary operations and API calls that consume resources.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs62 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs62{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2 Improved Responsiveness:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2  Immediate failure lets users or calling services react faster.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs62 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs62{\pntxtb \'95}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2 Simplified Error Handling:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2  Early detection makes issues easier to diagnose and resolve.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs56\cf2 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li540\fi-540\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\b\shad\f1\fs56\cf1 Handling Detected Failures (Cont.)\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1170\fi-450\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li540\fi-540 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs53 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs53{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs48\cf4 4.}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs48\cf2  Customer-Caused Errors and Service Limits\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li1710\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1170\fi-450 {\pntext\pard\plain\dbch\af2\loch\f4\fs53 \'95\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnfs53{\pntxtb \'95}}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs48\cf2 Validate user input early to prevent resource-intensive operations based on invalid requests.\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s4\li2250\fi-360\loch\af4\dbch\f2\fs34\cf3\lang1033\li1710 {\pntext\pard\plain\loch\af1\dbch\f6\fs48 \'a7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnfs48{\pntxtb \'a7}}{\b\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs48\cf2 Example:}{\dbch\af2\loch\f1\fs48\cf2  A service that retrieves accounts should cap requests at a reasonable limit (e.g., 5,000 accounts). If the request exceeds the limit, return an error immediately.\par 
